        "id": 6155
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-17T13:29:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the CPAL palette in COLRv0 and COLRv1 fonts currently only has 32-bit sRGB entries, but indeed, while we were designing COLRv1, we started having conversation about color definitions, better color interpolation, OpenType variations for CPAL etc. for a future version of the standard - not all of the conversation was capture in this issue, but one way to track it is here: https://github.com/googlefonts/colr-gradients-spec/issues/356",
